{"id": "EUVD-2026-96921", "enisaUuid": "a8fc6597-454e-31fc-9153-6d8178b26fb2", "description": "Abilityai Trinity through 0.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the Telegram router that allows agent-scoped MCP API keys to perform human-only binding operations. Attackers controlling an agent, typically via prompt injection, can send messages through the owner's bot token, replace the binding with their own token, or delete it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:57:52", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/rJ2OBa8sfl", "https://github.com/Abilityai/trinity/blob/e38c1c0f2567c602541c90c4c92152e99e6ead11/src/backend/routers/telegram.py#L168-L219", "https://github.com/Abilityai/trinity/blob/e38c1c0f2567c602541c90c4c92152e99e6ead11/src/backend/routers/telegram.py#L258-L323", "https://github.com/Abilityai/trinity", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/abilityai-trinity-through-0.9.5-missing-authorization-in-telegram-binding-routes"], "aliases": ["GHSA-65xq-cj8m-pqxc", "CVE-2026-108756"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "eb7518fc-5bcb-3dc6-81ba-08defee3fa22", "product": {"name": "trinity", "vendor": {"name": "Abilityai"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "62c4123a-dbaa-3224-9d77-c25191967548", "vendor": {"name": "Abilityai"}}], "isExploited": false}